From: local-fix
Subject: [PATCH] Do not drop media messages with an empty body

mautrix-telegram's relaybot/relay message handler rejects ANY Matrix
m.room.message event whose `content.body` is an empty string, via:

    elif not content.body:
        raise IgnoredMessageError("Message doesn't have a body")

This is correct for m.text (an empty text message is meaningless),
but it is wrong for media messages (m.image, m.audio, m.video,
m.file, m.sticker): several bridges - notably mautrix-whatsapp -
send `"body": ""` for media that has no caption, which is valid
per the Matrix spec (body is optional/empty for uncaptioned media).

The rejection happens before request logging/response, and is only
logged at DEBUG level on a per-portal logger, so from the outside
it looks like the media event vanishes silently: no error in
Telegram, no message in the room, nothing in default INFO logs.

Fix: only require a non-empty body for MessageType.TEXT. Media
messages already have their own body/filename fallback logic
further down in _handle_matrix_message (using content.filename
when body is absent), so this is safe.

--- a/mautrix_telegram/portal.py
+++ b/mautrix_telegram/portal.py
@@ -2286,7 +2286,7 @@ class Portal(DBPortal, BasePortal):
     ) -> None:
         if not content.msgtype:
             raise IgnoredMessageError("Message doesn't have a msgtype")
-        elif not content.body:
+        elif not content.body and content.msgtype == MessageType.TEXT:
             raise IgnoredMessageError("Message doesn't have a body")
 
         logged_in = not await sender.needs_relaybot(self)
